==Russian==

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|свято́й}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-святой.ogg}}

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|ru|orv|свѧтъ}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*svętъ}}, from {{der|ru|ine-pro|*ḱwen-||holy}}.

====Adjective====
{{ru-adj|свято́й|святе́е|святе́йший|adv=свя́то|absn=свя́тость}}

# [[holy]], [[sacred]] (dedicated to a religious purpose)
#* {{quote-song|ru|title= {{w|Whirlwinds of Danger|Warszawianka of 1905}}|year= {{circa|1897}}|origyear= 1883|composer= w:Józef Pławiński|lyricist= w:Gleb Krzhizhanovsky
|url= https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=enkzIm3BaH8
|text= На бой кровавый, '''святой''' и правый!<br>Марш, марш вперёд, рабочий народ!
|translation= To the bloody fight, '''holy''' and just!<br>March, march forth, working folk!}}

